# Docker-only development

All work on this repository must run inside Docker. Do not install project dependencies on the host (no `pip`, `venv`, `pytest`, `ruff`, or PySide6 on the host).

## How to work

```bash
docker compose build
docker compose run --rm dev bash
docker compose run --rm dev python -m pytest
docker compose run --rm dev python -m ruff check .
```

After changing `pyproject.toml`, rebuild:

```bash
docker compose build --no-cache
```

Test comics: `/comics` in the container (`CC_TEST_COMICS` in `.env`, currently `/home/prime/Temp/PageMaster-Test-Content`).

## Do not

- Create or use a host `.venv/`
- Run `pip install` or `python -m venv` on the host
- Document host-only setup without a Docker path
